## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design comprehensive end-to-end testing strategies for complex multi-tenant systems involving schema evolution, feature flags, distributed caching, and failure resilience at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Contract testing and schema compatibility across tenant boundaries
- Feature flag management and canary deployment strategies
- Distributed caching consistency with Redis TTL management
- Chaos engineering and failure injection patterns
- Performance testing under high concurrency scenarios
- Observability and monitoring in multi-tenant architectures

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test using k6 with dynamic flag injection
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';

export let options = {
  vus: 2000,
  duration: '5m',
};

export default function () {
  const tenantId = Math.floor(Math.random() * 100);
  const userId = Math.floor(Math.random() * 10000);
  const url = `https://api.example.com/api/v2/users/${userId}`;

  const params = {
    headers: {
      'X-Tenant-ID': tenantId.toString(),
      'X-Feature-Flags': `extendedProfile:${Math.random() > 0.5}`
    }
  };

  const response = http.get(url, params);
  check(response, {
    'status is 200': (r) => r.status === 200,
    'response time < 200ms': (r) => r.timings.duration < 200,
    'valid schema': (r) => validateSchema(r.json())
  });

  sleep(0.1);
}
```

